	shorttitle = {Kinetic theory of point vortices},
	url = {http://link.aps.org/doi/10.1103/PhysRevE.64.026309},
	doi = {10.1103/PhysRevE.64.026309},
	abstract = {We develop a kinetic theory for point vortices in two-dimensional hydrodynamics. Using standard projection operator techniques, we derive a Fokker-Planck equation describing the relaxation of a {\textquotedblleft}test{\textquotedblright} vortex in a bath of {\textquotedblleft}field{\textquotedblright} vortices at statistical equilibrium. The relaxation is due to the combined effect of a diffusion and a drift. The drift is shown to be responsible for the organization of point vortices at negative temperatures. A description that goes beyond the thermal bath approximation is attempted. A new kinetic equation is obtained which respects all conservation laws of the point vortex system and satisfies a H theorem. Close to equilibrium, this equation reduces to the ordinary Fokker-Planck equation.},
